rem ACMP 0586 - Bill (Законопроект)
rem Determine which bill passes in parliament using backward induction game theory.
rem
rem Deputies vote rationally with full information on preferences.
rem Voting proceeds sequentially from bill 1 to bill K.
rem If all K bills are rejected, Crisis occurs (the worst outcome for all deputies).
rem Thus, if bill K is reached, it is guaranteed to pass (outcome is K).
rem By backward induction from bill K-1 down to 1:
rem When voting on bill I, rejecting it leads to NextOutcome.
rem A deputy votes FOR bill I if they prefer I over NextOutcome.
rem If at least M deputies vote FOR, bill I passes (NextOutcome becomes I).

use io
use cli
use sequences
use numbers
use text

arg Input text = "3 2 4\n3 4 1 2\n2 3 4 1\n4 1 2 3"

Tokens = (Input split "\n" join " ") split " "
Tokens = Tokens (Tokens not equal "")
Nums = Tokens integer

N = Nums 0
M = Nums 1
K = Nums 2

Rank = array shape N K fill 0
PosOrder = (0 till K) array

for D in 0 till N
  Prefs = Nums ((D * K + 3) till ((D + 1) * K + 3))
  Row = array shape K fill 0
  Row (Prefs - 1) = PosOrder
  Rank D = Row
end

NextOutcome = K - 1

if K greater 1
  for I in ((0 till (K - 1)) array) reverse
    ColI = Rank # I
    ColNext = Rank # NextOutcome
    Votes = (ColI less ColNext) count
    if Votes greater (M - 1)
      NextOutcome = I
    end
  end
end

Answer = (NextOutcome + 1) text
Answer print
